  "claims": [
    "Active explorationShare now governs supplied-source and hypothesis-analysis admission through the existing atomic storage transaction. The default setting was previously stored without an admission consumer.",
    "Reference policy exploration-admitted-work:1 reserves floor(jobsPerDay * explorationShare) slots in the rolling 24-hour charged-work budget. With at least two currently permitted approved topics, reserved slots admit a topic tied for the fewest charged attempts. Counts measure work allocation, never interest, truth or source reliability.",
    "Failed, cancelled and interrupted admissions remain charged; exact retries return the same work without another charge. Rejections do not insert work. Topic use still requires all prior current-owner, privacy, source, budget and provider gates. No network request or job is automatically created.",
    "No competing eligible approved topic releases the reserve. Missing or erased charged-work topic payload makes reserved coverage unavailable until that charge expires; private topic history is not reconstructed or copied into a new store.",
    "Tests cover retries, failures, restart, rolling expiry, foreign scope, erased payload, invalid shares, zero/sub-slot rounding, the full 256-topic configured bound, active settings and current exclusions. Control-page help explains whole slots and lack of automatic networking."
  ],
